<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serrata del Maggior Consiglio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1297</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Serrata del Maggior Consiglio ('closing of the Great Council') was a reform of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> begun in 1297 under Doge Pietro Gradenigo. It limited membership of the Great Council to men whose families had recently sat on it and a few co-opted families, and in the following decades membership became hereditary. It created the closed Venetian patriciate, later registered in the Golden Book.</p></div>
